I get off the bus at the big, busy square.
There are people everywhere, and I am not entirely sure of the way.
I walk over to a friendly, older woman to ask for help.
"Excuse me," I say, "how do I get down to the harbour?"
The woman points down the street.
"Walk straight ahead from here, and turn left down by the bakery," she says.
"Then you will enter the old streets," she adds.
I say thank you very much for the help.
I begin my walk down toward the old neighbourhood.
